# Each line: an upstream file, and why it does not measure node:perf_hooks here.
test-perf-hooks-histogram.js: cross-module integration; posts a histogram through a MessageChannel twice, and node's JSTransferable protocol rebuilds it on the receiving side by loading node's own internal/histogram, so the received object is never this module's; every other assertion in the file, including the event loop delay monitor's, is kept in local/histogram-static.js
test-performance-gc.js: cross-module integration; `gc` entries are produced by node's performance binding from V8's garbage-collection callbacks after `global.gc()`, engine instrumentation outside the profile (it has no v8 module); observing the `gc` type is accepted and covered by test-performanceobserver-gc.js and test-perf-gc-crash.js
test-performance-gc-minor-ms.js: cross-module integration; same V8 garbage-collection instrumentation as test-performance-gc.js, driven by `gcUntil` and `--expose-gc`
test-performance-nodetiming.js: runner limitation; asserts `loopStart === -1` and `idleTime === 0` at the top level, which holds only on the main script's first tick, and this runner evaluates a test body after node's loop has started; every other assertion in the file is kept in local/nodetiming-static.js
test-performance-nodetiming-uvmetricsinfo.js: host-binary subprocess; runs `process.execPath` on a fixture that loads node's own perf_hooks, so it passes with the module blanked, and routing the fixture through the runner would evaluate its first-tick zero-metrics assertions after the loop started; the metrics' shape and a loop iteration counting are asserted in local/nodetiming-static.js
test-perf-hooks-worker-timeorigin.js: cross-module integration; the Worker is node's own isolate reading node's performance, compared against the time origin this module's stand-in forwards from node, so it passes with the module blanked; `timeOrigin` against `Date.now() - performance.now()` is asserted in local/nodetiming-static.js
test-performance-many-marks.js: asserts nothing; marks a million names and clears them, and passes with the module blanked; the buffer warning those marks provoke is asserted in local/buffer-warning-static.js
